From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:52:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] WebContent: Launch ImageDecoder on first decode and retire it
 when idle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A page with no images was starting an ImageDecoder (~23 MiB RSS plus any
decoded-image heap) with every WebContent process. Install the codec
plugin empty, ask the Browser for a decoder on the first decode_image(),
and drop the client after 15 s with no pending decodes or animation
sessions so the process can exit. A later image starts a new decoder.
Measured github.com −66 MiB PSS and x.com −22 MiB PSS vs the decommit
keepers; youtube.com is page-variance-limited.
